From: BSP Maintainers <bsp@example.com>
Subject: [PATCH] demos: wait for XDG shell header before compiling C++

The OpenCV demo includes xdg-shell-client-protocol.h, but its object
files do not depend on that generated header on the first build.
Parallel make can compile main.cpp while wayland-scanner is writing
it, resulting in missing XDG shell declarations.

Add the header prerequisite to the C++ objects.

Upstream-Status: Pending

--- a/demos/imx-camera-rotation-opencv/Makefile
+++ b/demos/imx-camera-rotation-opencv/Makefile
@@ -57,6 +57,9 @@
 %.o: %.cpp
 	$(CXX) $(CXXFLAGS) -c $< -o $@ -MD -MP
 
+# C++ sources include the generated client protocol header.
+$(CPP_OBJECTS): $(OUTPUT_HEADER)
+
 # Explicit rule for xdg-shell-client-protocol.o
 $(OUTPUT_CODE:.c=.o): $(OUTPUT_CODE) $(OUTPUT_HEADER)
 	$(CC) $(CFLAGS) -c $(OUTPUT_CODE) -o $@ -MD -MP
